 o, e, t, i, l, a, s, r, the end code ($00, code $0A), h, newline, y, u, '.', m, p, k, g, c, {06}, {03}, w, v, d, {07}, {0B}, x, q, '?', '=', '!', {08}; codes $00-$1D give entries $00-$1D, the escape code $1F followed by 0-3 gives entries $1E-$21, and code $1E is the capital shift; $22-$3B are unused $7F.","t":"byte","b":[32,110,111,101,116,105,108,97]},{"a":52376,"t":"byte","b":[115,114,0,104,13,121,117,46]},{"a":52384,"t":"byte","b":[109,112,107,103,99,6,3,119]},{"a":52392,"t":"byte","b":[118,100,7,11,120,113,63,61]},{"a":52400,"t":"byte","b":[33,8,127,127,127,127,127,127]},{"a":52408,"t":"byte","b":[127,127,127,127,127,127,127,127]},{"a":52416,"t":"byte","b":[127,127,127,127,127,127,127,127]},{"a":52424,"t":"byte","b":[127,127,127,127]},{"a":52428,"l":"library_text_groups","c":"The library text's group table: offsets from $CCCC to the groups of four messages, +$08 = $CCD4 (messages 0-3), +$5C = $CD28 (4-7), +$9F = $CD6B (8-11). The fourth word, $74A6 at $CCD2, would point outside the block; nothing asks for messages 12-15.","t":"word","b":[8,0,92,0,159,0,166,116],"d":[8,92,159,29862]},{"a":52436,"l":"library_text_msgs_0_3","c":"Library messages 0-3, one bit stream: 0 empty (never printed); 1 '{07}You have too much on your mind to learn anything.\\n{06}' (no skill points, $CA5F); 2 '{07}Not even Einstein can learn anymore.\\n{06}' (no empty skill pair, $CA6E); 3 '\\n   IQ PTS LVL   SKILL\\n', the list header ($CA82). {07} opens the text window, {06} waits at '(RETURN)'.","t":"byte","b":[74,251,38,28,88,7,15,64]},{"a":52444,"t":"byte","b":[132,0,208,209,5,68,0,77]},{"a":52452,"t":"byte","b":[184,4,96,9,25,16,1,204]},{"a":52460,"t":"byte","b":[56,41,128,19,26,89,37,204]},{"a":52468,"t":"byte","b":[199,170,210,62,8,2,6,30]},{"a":52476,"t":"byte","b":[1,248,81,2,34,163,4,64]},{"a":52484,"t":"byte","b":[79,0,102,156,20,192,9,13]},{"a":52492,"t":"byte","b":[138,52,30,171,138,1,0,124]},{"a":52500,"t":"byte","b":[241,29,248,232,137,71,192,27]},{"a":52508,"t":"byte","b":[143,189,1,0,120,228,165,47]},{"a":52516,"t":"byte","b":[222,120,195,20]},{"a":52520,"l":"library_text_msgs_4_7","c":"Library messages 4-7: 4 'Skill points = {03}{08}' (show_skill_points); 5 'Who wants to enter?\\n' ($CA24); 6 '\\n{0B} is in no condition to learn.\\n{06}' (the member is not conscious, $CA38; {0B} is the name); 7 'Not enough skill points!{03}' ($CAAD).","t":"byte","b":[30,201,98,12,136,162,4,130]},{"a":52528,"t":"byte","b":[192,15,192,254,161,252,93,2]},{"a":52536,"t":"byte","b":[220,19,8,2,68,128,17,200]},{"a":52544,"t":"byte","b":[72,31,48,197,54,40,8,148]},{"a":52552,"t":"byte","b":[0,130,0,84,132,92,72,17]},{"a":52560,"t":"byte","b":[1,16,1,204,56,41,60,86]},{"a":52568,"t":"byte","b":[149,15,130,128,17,132,155,11]},{"a":52576,"t":"byte","b":[32,89,140,1,81,148,64,208]},{"a":52584,"t":"byte","b":[23,86,1]},{"a":52587,"l":"library_text_msgs_8_10","c":"Library messages 8-10, the last it prints: 8 'You know it all.{03}' (level 255, $CAC8); 9 '{07}{0B} is not smart enough to learn anything here.\\n{06}' (no skill on offer within the member's IQ, $CAC0); 10 'Need more experience.{03}' (level not below the rank, $CACC). Message 10's end code is in $CDA4.","t":"byte","b":[190,9,7,100,16,23,20,2]},{"a":52595,"t":"byte","b":[142,49,207,42,189,65,65,32]},{"a":52603,"t":"byte","b":[8,2,16,60,137,128,17,132]},{"a":52611,"t":"byte","b":[155,11,16,1,204,56,41,128]},{"a":52619,"t":"byte","b":[19,26,89,37,76,176,70,26]},{"a":52627,"t":"byte","b":[143,85,229,195,24,25,64,145]},{"a":52635,"t":"byte","b":[6,24,60,142,84,70,160,227]},{"a":52643,"t":"byte","b":[89,5]},{"a":52645,"l":"library_last_byte","c":"The last byte module 2's own packed data decodes to ($D0): its 847 packed bytes, the same on sides 2, 3 and 4, give $CA00-$CDA5, 934 bytes. It follows message 10's end code ($CDA4) and nothing reads it: the library prints messages 1-10 only, and no instruction or pointer in the module reaches past $CDA4.","t":"byte","b":[208]},{"a":52646,"t":"gap","n":12890},{"a":52646,"t":"note","l":"library_tail","c":"$CDA6-$CF3E: not module 2. The unpacker decodes a 4-page read window ($CE), not the stream's length, and on side 2 (this snapshot) module 2's 847 packed bytes end at byte $9A of T33/L3. The window reads on through the rest of that sector, 101 bytes equal to the last 101 of side 2's item table (entry 2 of T35/L15, T33/L16-L14: item 82's bytes 3-7, then items 83-94, of which 83, 84 and 85 are alike, DC 05 00 90 00 00 01 00), which give $CDA6-$CEEF, and the first 76 bytes of T33/L2, where tile set 2's stream begins, which give $CEF0-$CF3E; all are decoded here with module 2's table. Nothing reads them.","note":"outside the tracked image"}]}